1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,414
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,506
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,556 --> 00:00:18,652
The Story of the Out-of-Tune Road Band!

7
00:00:23,223 --> 00:00:29,006
Once upon a time, on a tiny little
farm, there lived a gray donkey named

8
00:00:29,056 --> 00:00:30,256
Theodore.

9
00:00:30,441 --> 00:00:34,550
He had long ears, kind
eyes, and a very big voice.

10
00:00:35,216 --> 00:00:39,824
For many years, Theodore carried
sacks of corn to the mill.

11
00:00:40,133 --> 00:00:45,033
But now his back was tired, and the
farmer had found a younger donkey.

12
00:00:45,730 --> 00:00:50,810
Theodore let out a long, deep sigh
as he looked at the winding road.

13
00:00:51,383 --> 00:00:56,911
I can't carry heavy sacks anymore, but
my voice is still as strong as thunder,

14
00:00:56,961 --> 00:00:59,944
Theodore said, puffing out his chest.

15
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:04,980
And, to prove it, he let
out a long, loud bray.

16
00:01:08,154 --> 00:01:13,679
Up on the fence, Popcorn the little
owl nearly tumbled backwards.

17
00:01:14,257 --> 00:01:15,634
Hoo, hoo!

18
00:01:15,728 --> 00:01:18,632
What a mighty voice, Mister Theodore!

19
00:01:18,682 --> 00:01:21,845
Popcorn said, fluffing her feathers.

20
00:01:22,435 --> 00:01:23,861
I know what I'll do,

21
00:01:23,911 --> 00:01:25,619
Theodore said happily.

22
00:01:25,669 --> 00:01:30,363
I'll go to Flute Town, where
everyone plays music in the square.

23
00:01:30,623 --> 00:01:32,491
I'll become a singer there!

24
00:01:33,110 --> 00:01:38,038
And Popcorn, who loved an adventure,
decided to fly along with him.

25
00:01:39,118 --> 00:01:44,026
After a long walk, they found a
caramel-colored dog lying in the shade of a

26
00:01:44,076 --> 00:01:45,250
tree.

27
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:47,770
This little dog's name was Pitanga.

28
00:01:48,430 --> 00:01:53,691
Pitanga had her nose between her paws,
and her tail wasn't wagging at all.

29
00:01:54,273 --> 00:01:56,028
Why are you so sad?

30
00:01:56,078 --> 00:01:57,849
Theodore asked gently.

31
00:01:58,445 --> 00:02:02,420
I used to be the fastest dog on the
farm, but now the sheep run faster than I

32
00:02:02,470 --> 00:02:03,096
do,

33
00:02:03,146 --> 00:02:05,227
Pitanga answered quietly.

34
00:02:05,819 --> 00:02:08,178
Then come with us to Flute Town!

35
00:02:08,228 --> 00:02:10,307
Theodore said with a big grin.

36
00:02:10,357 --> 00:02:12,048
You can be our singer!

37
00:02:12,653 --> 00:02:16,039
Pitanga lifted her ears
and wagged her tail.

38
00:02:16,668 --> 00:02:19,416
And she barked twice, full of joy.

39
00:02:21,445 --> 00:02:26,575
A little farther on, on top of a stone
wall, a striped cat with enormous

40
00:02:26,625 --> 00:02:28,678
whiskers was taking a nap.

41
00:02:29,035 --> 00:02:31,533
His name was Whiskers, of course.

42
00:02:32,122 --> 00:02:36,286
Good morning, Mister Cat, you
look a little gloomy today,

43
00:02:36,336 --> 00:02:39,694
Popcorn said, tilting her little head.

44
00:02:40,237 --> 00:02:43,081
The lady of the house says
I don't catch mice anymore,

45
00:02:43,131 --> 00:02:45,388
Whiskers explained with a yawn.

46
00:02:45,438 --> 00:02:49,128
But I'd much rather nap in the
sunshine, thank you very much!

47
00:02:49,704 --> 00:02:52,904
Nobody in our band has to catch any mice,

48
00:02:52,954 --> 00:02:54,789
Theodore said with a laugh.

49
00:02:54,839 --> 00:02:57,576
You only have to sing with all your heart!

50
00:02:58,158 --> 00:03:01,877
Whiskers hopped down from
the wall and stretched very,

51
00:03:01,949 --> 00:03:03,363
very slowly.

52
00:03:04,019 --> 00:03:07,989
And he gave a lovely meow,
to show that he could sing.

53
00:03:10,429 --> 00:03:15,254
On the gate of the very last farm,
a rooster with a bright red comb was

54
00:03:15,304 --> 00:03:17,204
crowing and crowing.

55
00:03:17,552 --> 00:03:21,758
It was Crispin, the loudest
rooster for miles around.

56
00:03:24,236 --> 00:03:26,411
What's all that noise, my friend?

57
00:03:26,461 --> 00:03:28,527
Theodore asked curiously.

58
00:03:29,096 --> 00:03:33,129
I sing every morning, but the farm folks
complain that I wake everybody up too

59
00:03:33,179 --> 00:03:33,866
early,

60
00:03:33,916 --> 00:03:36,733
Crispin replied, feeling grumpy.

61
00:03:37,314 --> 00:03:40,086
Well, in our band you can
sing whenever you like!

62
00:03:40,136 --> 00:03:42,939
Pitanga said, wagging her tail.

63
00:03:43,541 --> 00:03:47,760
Crispin flapped his wings and
hopped onto Theodore's back.

64
00:03:48,430 --> 00:03:52,171
So the four of them decided to
have their very first rehearsal,

65
00:03:52,221 --> 00:03:54,191
right there in the middle of the road.

66
00:03:57,924 --> 00:04:02,805
It was so out of tune, so terribly out
of tune, that a little bird covered its

67
00:04:02,855 --> 00:04:04,616
ears with its wings.

68
00:04:05,202 --> 00:04:06,578
Hoo, hoo!

69
00:04:06,674 --> 00:04:10,699
With a little practice, this
is going to sound wonderful!

70
00:04:10,749 --> 00:04:13,663
Popcorn said, trying not to giggle.

71
00:04:14,775 --> 00:04:19,105
Flute Town was very far
away, and night came softly.

72
00:04:19,277 --> 00:04:23,760
In the forest, the crickets
began to sing very quietly.

73
00:04:24,414 --> 00:04:28,897
The friends were tired, and their
tummies were rumbling with hunger.

74
00:04:29,533 --> 00:04:35,233
Popcorn, who can see very well in the
dark, flew up to the highest branch of a

75
00:04:35,283 --> 00:04:36,558
pine tree.

76
00:04:37,141 --> 00:04:38,518
Hoo, hoo!

77
00:04:38,627 --> 00:04:42,909
I can see a little lit-up window,
right there between the trees!

78
00:04:42,959 --> 00:04:46,595
Popcorn said, flapping her wings with joy.

79
00:04:47,255 --> 00:04:52,386
The friends tiptoed all the way to a
wooden cabin, with the smell of warm pie

80
00:04:52,436 --> 00:04:54,155
drifting out of the window.

81
00:04:55,284 --> 00:04:58,975
Theodore stretched his neck
and peeked through the window.

82
00:04:59,641 --> 00:05:05,763
Inside, two greedy raccoons were sitting
in front of a mountain of fruit pies.

83
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:09,548
Those are the pies for
the Flute Town festival!

84
00:05:09,598 --> 00:05:12,233
Popcorn whispered very quietly.

85
00:05:12,283 --> 00:05:16,016
These raccoons sneaked them
all away from the bakery!

86
00:05:16,694 --> 00:05:19,678
The friends came up
with a very clever plan.

87
00:05:20,388 --> 00:05:23,974
Theodore stood strong and
steady under the window.

88
00:05:24,318 --> 00:05:29,032
Pitanga climbed onto his back,
Whiskers climbed onto Pitanga's back,

89
00:05:29,082 --> 00:05:32,718
and Crispin perched at
the very top, on Whiskers.

90
00:05:33,356 --> 00:05:37,917
It was such a funny tower of animals
that Popcorn had to cover her beak to

91
00:05:37,967 --> 00:05:39,450
keep from laughing.

92
00:05:40,095 --> 00:05:45,134
When Popcorn flapped her wings, the
whole band sang at the same time,

93
00:05:45,193 --> 00:05:46,759
as loud as they could.

94
00:05:50,523 --> 00:05:55,126
The raccoons got such a fright that they
ran out the back door and disappeared

95
00:05:55,176 --> 00:05:56,548
into the forest.

96
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:04,795
And they left every single pie
behind, without a single bite taken.

97
00:06:05,873 --> 00:06:10,565
Early the next morning, the friends
carried the pies back to Flute Town.

98
00:06:11,206 --> 00:06:16,189
The baker, Rosa, gave them a
smile as big as the town square.

99
00:06:16,798 --> 00:06:18,705
You saved our festival!

100
00:06:18,755 --> 00:06:22,574
Rosa the baker said, with
happy tears in her eyes.

101
00:06:22,624 --> 00:06:24,913
Would you play a song for us?

102
00:06:25,543 --> 00:06:29,207
The band lined up on the
bandstand and began to play.

103
00:06:32,980 --> 00:06:37,430
It was still wonderfully out of tune,
but it was so full of joy that the

104
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:41,652
children, the grandparents, and even
the little dogs in the square started to

105
00:06:41,702 --> 00:06:42,902
dance.

106
00:06:43,381 --> 00:06:49,109
And Crispin, very proud of himself,
insisted on singing the ending all by

107
00:06:49,159 --> 00:06:50,359
himself.

108
00:06:53,315 --> 00:06:58,270
After the festival, the four friends
went back to the cabin in the forest.

109
00:06:58,918 --> 00:07:04,193
There was room for Theodore to rest his
back, sunshine for Whiskers to nap in,

110
00:07:04,321 --> 00:07:09,832
a cozy rug for Pitanga, and a tall
window for Crispin to watch the sunrise.

111
00:07:10,399 --> 00:07:13,322
I thought I was too old
to start something new,

112
00:07:13,372 --> 00:07:15,535
Theodore said with a smile.

113
00:07:16,085 --> 00:07:17,762
And now you have a whole band,

114
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:21,406
Pitanga answered, leaning
her head against him.

115
00:07:22,009 --> 00:07:27,324
Hoo, hoo... it's never too late to
start again, especially with friends by

116
00:07:27,374 --> 00:07:28,379
your side,

117
00:07:28,429 --> 00:07:30,759
Popcorn said very softly.

118
00:07:31,426 --> 00:07:36,598
And every night, the band of friends
played a very quiet rehearsal,

119
00:07:36,648 --> 00:07:38,923
just to sing the forest to sleep.

120
00:07:46,226 --> 00:07:47,426
The End.

121
00:07:49,133 --> 00:07:49,845
Hoo...

122
00:07:49,895 --> 00:07:50,920
Psst!

123
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:52,542
Are you still awake?

124
00:07:52,696 --> 00:07:54,749
Did you like tonight's story?

125
00:07:54,922 --> 00:07:59,794
Theodore and his friends showed us that
it is never too late to start again,

126
00:07:59,844 --> 00:08:02,601
and that together we are much stronger.

127
00:08:02,858 --> 00:08:07,164
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

128
00:08:07,460 --> 00:08:12,358
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

129
00:08:12,408 --> 00:08:14,813
for more stories at bedtime.

130
00:08:15,117 --> 00:08:16,317
Hoo...

